.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt LIBURING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm liburing
.Nd io_uring compatibility library backed by ioport/ioevent
.Sh LIBRARY
.Nm
library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In liburing.h
.In io_uring.h
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_queue_init "unsigned entries" "struct io_uring *ring" "unsigned flags"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_queue_init_params "unsigned entries" "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_params *p"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_queue_exit "struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_queue_mmap "int fd" "struct io_uring_params *p" "struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft struct io_uring_sqe *
.Fn io_uring_get_sqe "struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_submit "struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_submit_and_wait "struct io_uring *ring" "unsigned wait_nr"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_submit_and_get_events "struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_wait_cqe "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_cqe **cqe_ptr"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_wait_cqe_nr "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_cqe **cqe_ptr" "unsigned wait_nr"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_peek_cqe "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_cqe **cqe_ptr"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_peek_batch_cqe "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_cqe **cqes" "unsigned count"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_cqe_seen "struct io_uring *ring" "struct io_uring_cqe *cqe"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_cq_advance "struct io_uring *ring" "unsigned nr"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn io_uring_sq_ready "const struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn io_uring_sq_space_left "const struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn io_uring_cq_ready "const struct io_uring *ring"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_prep_rw "int op" "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe" "int fd" "const void *addr" "unsigned len" "__u64 offset"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_prep_read "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe" "int fd" "void *buf" "unsigned nbytes" "__u64 offset"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_prep_write "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe" "int fd" "const void *buf" "unsigned nbytes" "__u64 offset"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_prep_nop "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_sqe_set_data "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe" "void *data"
.Ft void
.Fn io_uring_sqe_set_flags "struct io_uring_sqe *sqe" "unsigned flags"
.Ft void *
.Fn io_uring_cqe_get_data "const struct io_uring_cqe *cqe"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_setup "unsigned entries" "struct io_uring_params *p"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_enter "int fd" "unsigned to_submit" "unsigned min_complete" "unsigned flags" "sigset_t *sig"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_enter2 "int fd" "unsigned to_submit" "unsigned min_complete" "unsigned flags" "sigset_t *sig" "size_t sz"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_register "int fd" "unsigned opcode" "const void *arg" "unsigned nr_args"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_major_version "void"
.Ft int
.Fn io_uring_minor_version "void"
.Ft bool
.Fn io_uring_check_version "int major" "int minor"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library provides a source-compatible subset of the Linux liburing queue API on
top of the native .Dx
.Xr ioport 2
and
.Xr ioevent 2
completion-port system calls, so that io_uring programs recompile unchanged.
The submission and completion queues live in ordinary user memory allocated by
the library; there is no Linux ring mmap and no shared kernel ring.
Only the basic single-operation read, write, and nop paths are provided.
Every Linux-specific operation that cannot be expressed faithfully fails
honestly rather than emulating partial semantics.
.Pp
The
.Nm
API reports the aligned upstream liburing release via
.Fn io_uring_major_version
and
.Fn io_uring_minor_version ;
the current release is 2.14.
.Ss Queue setup
.Fn io_uring_queue_init
creates a ring with
.Fa entries
submission queue slots, allocating the local submission and completion queues
and creating the underlying completion port.
The
.Fa flags
argument is reserved and must be zero.
.Fn io_uring_queue_init_params
is identical but fills
.Fa p
.Pq if non- Dv NULL
with the resulting ring parameters.
.Fn io_uring_queue_exit
closes the underlying port and frees the local queues.
.Pp
.Fn io_uring_queue_mmap
always fails with
.Er ENOSYS :
.Dx has no Linux ring mmap ABI.
.Ss Submission
.Fn io_uring_get_sqe
returns a pointer to the next available submission queue entry, or
.Dv NULL
if the submission queue is full.
The returned
.Vt struct io_uring_sqe
is filled in with one of the
.Fn io_uring_prep_*
helpers before being submitted.
.Pp
.Fn io_uring_submit
submits all prepared but not yet submitted entries.
Entries prepared with
.Fn io_uring_prep_nop
complete locally;
entries prepared with
.Fn io_uring_prep_read
or
.Fn io_uring_prep_write
are translated into
.Dv IO_READ
or
.Dv IO_WRITE
requests on the completion port.
.Fn io_uring_submit_and_wait
submits and then waits until at least
.Fa wait_nr
completions are ready.
.Fn io_uring_submit_and_get_events
submits and then reaps any already-available completions.
.Ss Completion
.Fn io_uring_wait_cqe
waits for one completion and returns it in
.Fa cqe_ptr ;
.Fn io_uring_wait_cqe_nr
waits until at least
.Fa wait_nr
completions are ready and returns the first in
.Fa cqe_ptr .
.Fn io_uring_peek_cqe
returns the next completion without blocking, or
.Er EAGAIN
if none is ready.
.Fn io_uring_peek_batch_cqe
fills
.Fa cqes
with up to
.Fa count
completion pointers and returns the number filled.
.Pp
.Fn io_uring_cqe_seen
marks one completion consumed;
.Fn io_uring_cq_advance
marks
.Fa nr
completions consumed.
.Fn io_uring_cq_ready
returns the number of completions ready in the local queue, and
.Fn io_uring_sq_ready
returns the number of prepared but unsubmitted submission entries, with
.Fn io_uring_sq_space_left
returning the remaining free slots.
.Ss Preparation helpers
The following are inline functions in
.In liburing.h .
.Fn io_uring_prep_read
and
.Fn io_uring_prep_write
prepare a read or write at
.Fa offset
of
.Fa nbytes
bytes to or from
.Fa buf ;
.Fn io_uring_prep_rw
is their common underlying helper.
.Fn io_uring_prep_nop
prepares a no-op.
.Fn io_uring_sqe_set_data
stores an opaque pointer in the entry, returned later by
.Fn io_uring_cqe_get_data .
.Fn io_uring_sqe_set_flags
sets the per-entry flags; only zero is currently supported.
.Ss Raw syscall wrappers
.Fn io_uring_setup ,
.Fn io_uring_enter ,
.Fn io_uring_enter2 ,
and
.Fn io_uring_register
are provided for ABI compatibility and always fail with
.Er ENOSYS ;
they never issue Linux-numbered system calls.
Programs that rely on the Linux ring file descriptor, ring mmap offsets, or
these raw entry points are outside the compatibility target.
.Ss Version
.Fn io_uring_major_version
and
.Fn io_uring_minor_version
return the aligned upstream liburing release numbers.
.Fn io_uring_check_version
returns
.Dv true
if the aligned release is at least
.Fa major . Fa minor .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The queue API functions return 0 or a positive value on success and a negative
errno value on failure, following the upstream liburing convention.
The raw syscall wrappers and
.Fn io_uring_queue_mmap
instead return -1 and set
.Va errno .
.Fn io_uring_get_sqe
returns a pointer or
.Dv NULL .
.Fn io_uring_sq_ready ,
.Fn io_uring_sq_space_left ,
and
.Fn io_uring_cq_ready
return unsigned counts.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
No completion is ready for
.Fn io_uring_peek_cqe .
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fn io_uring_queue_init
was called with zero
.Fa entries
or non-zero
.Fa flags .
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
Memory allocation for the local queues failed.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
A Linux-only raw wrapper or
.Fn io_uring_queue_mmap
was called.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
A submission queue entry requested an operation that is not implemented; it
completes with a negative
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
result in its completion.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioevent 2 ,
.Xr ioport 2
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
library first appeared in
.Dx 6.5 .
